{% from 'ingressroute.yml.j2' import monitoring_route with context %}
---
{#
  Two readers, and both read /api/v3/queue only: monitor-bridge's check_arr_queue (check.py)
  and postflight.py's §9.3 API-key check, which asks for this same path because it is the one
  this route admits. Nothing else on the sonarr API is reachable through this route.

  extra_client_cidrs adds daniel-box, the host postflight runs on. Without it postflight's §9.3
  check was structurally SKIP whenever sonarr's pod sat on daniel-server: the ClusterIP answers
  only a caller on the pod's own node, and this route admitted daniel-server alone, so the
  request fell through to sonarr's own Authelia'd route and 302'd (#1642). The path prefix, the
  LAN-only rule and sonarr's own X-Api-Key are unchanged.
#}
{{ monitoring_route(container_item.name, container_item.hostname, container_item.port, '/api/v3/queue',
                    extra_client_cidrs=[k8s_node_client_ip ~ '/32']) }}
